Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 16:23:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/33] =?UTF-8?q?headless:=20support=20adaptive=20sync=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20paint=20on=20the=20game's=20commit?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A headless gamescope composites on a synthetic vblank: the timer ticks
at -r and steamcompmgr samples whatever commit is ready. A frame that
finishes just after the sample waits out a full period, and mismatched
present/compose grids beat — so a consumer of the PipeWire node (a
remote-desktop/streaming host) receives measurably fewer unique frames
than the session rate. The workaround in the field is overdriving -r,
which makes the compositor (and a vsynced game) do the work twice to
throw half of it away.

The VRR machinery already does the right thing: with an active-VRR
connector, steamcompmgr treats every wakeup as a paint opportunity
(FlipType::VRR paints on hasRepaint; overlay-only repaints defer by
adaptive_sync_overlay_cycles), and the vblank timer swaps its draw-time
prediction for the flat kVRRFlushingTime redzone. Nothing about it is
DRM-specific — and a headless output is the ideal adaptive-sync
display, since its vblank is a fiction with no scanout to respect.

So let the headless connector participate: SupportsVRR() is true, and
IsVRRActive() is cv_adaptive_sync — with no scanout cycle to honor,
"supported" and "active" collapse into "asked for". The in-flight
present guard stays inert (headless Present() completes immediately
and queues nothing).

One real interaction: the VRR framerate limiter skips itself when the
target is within 2 Hz of the refresh rate, deferring to the display's
own pacing. A display that paces nothing must not be deferred to — on
headless the limiter is the only throttle the focused app has, and
skipping it turns every FIFO game loose to render as fast as it can.
PacesPresents() (default true, headless false) makes that deference
conditional, so --framerate-limit at the session rate keeps the game
paced while every present it does make is painted — and published to
PipeWire — the moment it lands.
---
 src/Backends/HeadlessBackend.cpp | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/backend.h                    |  6 ++++++
 src/meson.build                  |  3 ++-
 src/steamcompmgr.cpp             |  6 ++++++
 4 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Backends/HeadlessBackend.cpp b/src/Backends/HeadlessBackend.cpp
index 3168c88..1de1540 100644
--- a/src/Backends/HeadlessBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/HeadlessBackend.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@ extern int g_nPreferredOutputWidth;
 extern int g_nPreferredOutputHeight;
 // `--custom-refresh-rates` (main.cpp): the rates this virtual display may switch between.
 extern std::vector<uint32_t> g_customRefreshRates;
+// `--adaptive-sync` / Steam's gamescope_control toggle (steamcompmgr.cpp).
+extern gamescope::ConVar<bool> cv_adaptive_sync;
 
 namespace gamescope
 {
@@ -52,14 +54,32 @@ namespace gamescope
         }
 		virtual bool IsVRRActive() const override
 		{
-			return false;
+			// Engaged purely by request (`--adaptive-sync`, or Steam's toggle through
+			// gamescope_control): a headless output has no scanout cycle to honor, so
+			// "supported" and "active" collapse into "asked for".
+			return cv_adaptive_sync;
 		}
         virtual std::span<const BackendMode> GetModes() const override
         {
             return m_Modes;
         }
 
+        // A headless output is the ideal adaptive-sync display: its vblank is synthetic
+        // (no scanout exists to be respected), so nothing stops a paint from following the
+        // game's commit immediately. Without this, the compose timer quantizes game
+        // presents onto a fictional grid — a frame finished just after the paint sampled
+        // waits out a full period, and a consumer of the PipeWire node (a streaming host)
+        // receives fewer unique frames than the session rate.
         virtual bool SupportsVRR() const override
+        {
+            return true;
+        }
+
+        // Present() above completes instantly and queues nothing, so this connector paces
+        // nobody — see PacesPresents() in backend.h. With VRR active the framerate limiter
+        // is therefore the ONLY pace the focused app has; steamcompmgr consults this
+        // before letting "target ≈ refresh" stand the limiter down.
+        virtual bool PacesPresents() const override
         {
             return false;
         }
diff --git a/src/backend.h b/src/backend.h
index bd57c42..b7a7bfb 100644
--- a/src/backend.h
+++ b/src/backend.h
@@ -187,6 +187,12 @@ namespace gamescope
 
         virtual bool SupportsVRR() const = 0;
 
+        // Whether this connector's Present() itself paces flips — a real display's
+        // vblank/VRR cycle, or a nested host compositor's throttle. `false` means presents
+        // complete immediately (headless), so any pacing must come from software: the
+        // framerate limiter must never stand down in deference to such a "display".
+        virtual bool PacesPresents() const { return true; }
+
         virtual std::span<const uint8_t> GetRawEDID() const = 0;
         virtual std::span<const uint32_t> GetValidDynamicRefreshRates() const = 0;
 
diff --git a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
index a478ab0..22892af 100644
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -190,7 +190,8 @@ vcs_tag = run_command(vcs_tag_cmd, check: false).stdout().strip()
 #   +pfhdr6 — …and GAMESCOPE_NO_FOCUS windows are never focus candidates (no new capability)
 #   +pfhdr7 — …and PipeWire teardown cannot SIGSEGV a lingering compositor (no new capability)
 #   +pfhdr8 — …and the seat's keyboard carries the XKB_DEFAULT_* keymap (honours the box layout)
-version_tag = vcs_tag + '+pfhdr8' + ' (' + compiler_name + ' ' + compiler_version + ')'
+#   +pfhdr9 — …and the headless connector supports adaptive sync (paint on game commit)
+version_tag = vcs_tag + '+pfhdr9' + ' (' + compiler_name + ' ' + compiler_version + ')'
 
 gamescope_version_conf = configuration_data()
 gamescope_version_conf.set('VCS_TAG', version_tag)
diff --git a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
index 4e01613..edcb418 100644
--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -6916,6 +6916,12 @@ static bool steamcompmgr_should_vblank_window( bool bShouldLimitFPS, uint64_t vb
 	{
 		bool bCloseEnough = std::abs( g_nSteamCompMgrTargetFPS - nRefreshHz ) < 2;
 
+		// "Close enough to the refresh rate" skips the limiter in deference to the
+		// display's own pacing. A connector that does not pace presents (headless)
+		// offers no such deference — the limiter is the only pace there, at any target.
+		if ( !GetBackend()->GetCurrentConnector()->PacesPresents() )
+			bCloseEnough = false;
+
 		if ( g_nSteamCompMgrTargetFPS && bShouldLimitFPS && w && !bCloseEnough )
 		{
 			uint64_t schedule = w->last_commit_first_latch_time + g_SteamCompMgrLimitedAppRefreshCycle;
